      "title": "Pytest Mental Model and Assertions",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Pytest Mental Model and Assertions",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What pytest Runs",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Files",
                    "sub": "test_*.py or *_test.py",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Functions",
                    "sub": "test_*",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Classes",
                    "sub": "Test*, no `__init__`",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A test ==passes== if it finishes without raising",
                "A bare `assert` is enough",
                "pytest ==rewrites assert== to show both sides of a failed comparison"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Asserting Errors and Floats",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import pytest",
                "def test_err():",
                "    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=r\"invalid literal\") as exc:",
                "        int(\"abc\")",
                "    assert \"abc\" in str(exc.value)",
                "def test_float():",
                "    assert 0.1 + 0.2 == pytest.approx(0.3)"
              ],
              "note": "approx, because exact float equality fails"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`match` uses ==re.search==, not a full match",
                "`as exc` then `exc.value` gives the exception",
                "{red:Exact float ==} fails: use `pytest.approx`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "assert (x == 1, \"msg\")  # always true",
                "assert x == 1, \"msg\"    # correct"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Parentheses trap",
              "text": "`assert (x, 'message')` is a ==non-empty tuple==, so it is **always true**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Fixtures and Parametrize",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Fixtures and Parametrize",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Fixtures and Scope",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`@pytest.fixture` = setup; a test names it as an argument, return value ==injected==",
                "`yield`: before = setup, after = ==teardown==, runs even if the test fails",
                "Wider scope = {red:shared state}, risk of leaks"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "@pytest.fixture",
                "def conn():",
                "    c = connect()",
                "    yield c",
                "    c.close()"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "scope=",
                "Built"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`'function'` (default)",
                  "per test"
                ],
                [
                  "`'class'`",
                  "per class"
                ],
                [
                  "`'module'`",
                  "per file"
                ],
                [
                  "`'session'`",
                  "once per run"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Sharing and Parametrize",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`conftest.py`: fixtures for its folder and below, ==no import==",
                "`tmp_path`: built-in per-test temp directory",
                "`parametrize` runs ==one test per tuple==; `ids` names them",
                "Stack two decorators = {purple:cross product}"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"a,b,expected\", [(1,2,3),(2,3,5)], ids=[\"s\",\"m\"])",
                "def test_add(a, b, expected):",
                "    assert a + b == expected"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mutable wide fixture",
              "text": "One test mutates it, the next breaks. Keep it ==function-scoped== or copy it."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Does teardown run if the test fails?** Yes, code after `yield` always runs",
                "**Why avoid wide scopes?** Shared state leaks between tests",
                "**Where do shared fixtures live?** `conftest.py`, no import needed"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Monkeypatch and Mocking",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Monkeypatch and Mocking",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Monkeypatch",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`setattr`, `setenv`, `delenv`, `setitem`, `chdir` are ==undone automatically== after the test",
                "{green:Patch where the name is looked up}, not where it is defined",
                "`app.py` does `from time import sleep` → patch `app.sleep`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "def test_fast(monkeypatch):",
                "    monkeypatch.setattr('app.sleep', lambda s: None)",
                "    monkeypatch.setenv('MODE', 'test')",
                "    monkeypatch.chdir('/tmp')"
              ],
              "note": "all reverted when the test ends"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Mock Objects",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`Mock` / `MagicMock` ==records calls== made to it",
                "`m.return_value` sets the result",
                "`m.side_effect = Exception('x')` **raises**",
                "`side_effect = [1, 2]` returns values ==in order=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Check",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`m.assert_called_once_with(args)`",
                  "one call, exactly these args"
                ],
                [
                  "`m.call_count`",
                  "number of calls"
                ],
                [
                  "`m.call_args`",
                  "args of the last call"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`mocker.patch('pkg.mod.func')` (pytest-mock) = `unittest.mock.patch`",
                "It ==cleans up on its own==; the `patch` context manager works too"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Over-mocking",
              "text": "It tests the mock, not your code. Mock only ==I/O boundaries==: network, clock, disk. Use `autospec=True` so wrong signatures fail."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
